Z||000006||AL||12-18-1999||12:51 AM||||hey dog, on your starter where you put the shims, you should be able to see where they grinded the starter.well once you've seen that then add shims to fill in that space where the shims go, once it evens out flush then put it in and it should work fine.||||reg||1
Z||000007||dogtired||12-20-1999||03:10 AM||||Well today out in the snow, not really, I pulled it in the garage. I added another shimm to my starter? It now sounds lots better, starts every time and seems to be OK.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>That makes me a happy camper.<P>I really want to thank everyone here for the help and support, even MonkeyMan   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>ROFLMAO I think that helped more than anything. If I can't keep my since of Humor while working on these little treasures, I might as well buy a FORD  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>This is the GREATEST Forum, If you think I talk too much, just let me know. I won't change anything but at least you got to say something.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
